---
/**
 * The theme override control (#92): a fixed editorial chip, bottom right,
 * cycling system -> light/dark override -> back to system. Standalone by
 * design and mounted from BaseLayout, never from EditorialHeader (that
 * component is owned by parallel work). All state semantics, persistence,
 * and the after-swap re-stamp live in src/scripts/theme.ts; the pre-paint
 * gate in BaseLayout stamps html[data-theme] so a stored override never
 * flashes.
 *
 * This component carries markup + style only, no <script>: theme.ts is
 * imported by BaseLayout's single hydration point alongside terminal.ts, per
 * the one-deferred-module contract in that file. The control is a singleton
 * mounted once from the layout, so it never needs its own entry.
 *
 * The visible label always reflects the current state with zero JS: all
 * three labels are server-rendered and CSS keyed on html[data-theme] shows
 * exactly one. display:none drops the hidden two from the accessible name
 * as well, so the button's name ("theme: system" / "theme: light" /
 * "theme: dark") is correct from first paint, before any script runs, and
 * speech-input users can say exactly what they see.
 *
 * Material: the control recolors the PAGE, so it sits on the page ground in
 * the bracket-control idiom; it is never phosphor (#67: phosphor is the
 * machine's material, and the machine ignores this control). Hidden on
 * /chat: the expanded slab is always-night, so a theme control there would
 * visibly do nothing (#91 exempts /chat from editorial chrome the same way).
 *
 * Copy: bracket-label tokens stay lowercase (#76); no dashes (#18); never
 * the t-word in visitor-facing copy (#58).
 */
---

<button type="button" class="themectl" id="themectl">
  <span class="br" aria-hidden="true">[</span><span class="lbl"
    ><span class="tlab tlab-system">theme: system</span><span
      class="tlab tlab-light">theme: light</span
    ><span class="tlab tlab-dark">theme: dark</span></span
  ><span class="br" aria-hidden="true">]</span>
</button>

<style>
  .themectl {
    position: fixed;
    right: 12px;
    bottom: calc(10px + env(safe-area-inset-bottom, 0px));
    z-index: 40; /* above page content, always below the #wipe cover (99) */
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    min-height: 44px;
    padding: 0 10px;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 7px;
    background: var(--ground);
    color: var(--dim); /* the brackets */
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 12.5px;
    cursor: pointer;
  }
  .lbl {
    color: var(--accent);
  }
  /* the unified bracket-control treatment (terminal.css): label fills with
     the accent on hover/focus-visible, brackets stay put */
  .themectl:hover .lbl,
  .themectl:focus-visible .lbl {
    background: var(--accent);
    color: var(--on-accent);
  }

  /* one visible label, keyed on the pre-paint html[data-theme] stamp */
  .tlab {
    display: none;
  }
  :global(html:not([data-theme])) .tlab-system,
  :global(html[data-theme="light"]) .tlab-light,
  :global(html[data-theme="dark"]) .tlab-dark {
    display: inline;
  }

  /* /chat is the expanded slab: always night, nothing editorial to recolor,
     and the chip would float over the phosphor screen */
  :global(body:has([data-screen="chat"])) .themectl {
    display: none;
  }
</style>
